    "title": "Bibb resigns from O'Fallon City Council - NewsBreak",
    "text": "midriversnewsmagazine.com\nwebsite\nO'Fallon\nBibb resigns from O’Fallon City Council\nBy Ruby Keller,\n11 hours agoNathan Bibb announced his resignation from the O’Fallon City Council at its Sept. 11 meeting. On Aug. 24, in a 6-3 vote the council approved an agreement between the city and Wright Construction Services Inc. for phase 2 of the Center of Advanced Skills Training in Law Enforcement (CASTLE) in an amount not to exceed $23.5 million. Bibb, who is a vice president with Wright Construction, had recused himself from the vote that night, but the agreement drew criticism from the community and members of the council.",
